# American English spelling

All prose uses American spelling: the paper (`discover-v1/`), the response letter and tracker
(`OTHER/discover-v1-tist-reviews/`), text that generators print into tables and figures
(`tist_revision/pipeline/*.py`), and docs.

| ❌ British | ✅ American |
|---|---|
| neighbour, behaviour, colour, favour | neighbor, behavior, color, favor |
| labelled, labelling, unlabelled, modelled, modelling | labeled, labeling, unlabeled, modeled, modeling |
| standardise(d), normalise(d), initialise(d), optimise(r), minimise, maximise, summarise, harmonise, tokenisation | standardize(d), normalize(d), initialize(d), optimize(r), minimize, maximize, summarize, harmonize, tokenization |
| analyse (verb), centre, grey | analyze, center, gray |

Notes:
- "analyses" as the plural noun is correct; keep it.
- Don't rename code identifiers, file names or CSV columns just for spelling; fix only user-facing text.
- Text quoted from reviewers stays as written.
